---

<article class="space-y-8 text-gray-700 leading-8">
    <header class="space-y-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">
            OnnaSoft · Business technology
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-gray-900 md:text-5xl">
            Privacy Policy: We Protect Your Data Responsibly and Transparently
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-gray-500">
            At OnnaSoft, we are committed to protecting your privacy and
            handling your personal information responsibly. This Privacy Policy
            explains how we collect, use, store, and protect your data when you
            visit our website, contact our team, or use our technology services.
        </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Our Commitment to Your Privacy
        </h2>
        <p>
            We believe that trust is essential to every successful business
            relationship. That is why we approach data privacy with
            transparency, accountability, and security at every stage of our
            work. Our goal is to ensure that you understand what information we
            collect, why we need it, and how we handle it.
        </p>
        <p>
            OnnaSoft applies appropriate technical and organizational measures
            to help protect personal information against unauthorized access,
            loss, alteration, disclosure, or misuse. We continually seek to
            improve our practices as technology, business requirements, and
            applicable regulations evolve.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>
            Depending on how you interact with OnnaSoft, we may collect
            information that you voluntarily provide, including your name,
            business email address, telephone number, company name, and the
            details you submit through contact forms, service inquiries, or
            other communications.
        </p>
        <p>
            When you browse our website, certain technical information may also
            be collected, such as your IP address, browser type, device
            information, pages visited, and general usage data. Where
            applicable, cookies and similar technologies may help us understand
            website performance and improve your browsing experience.
        </p>
        <p>
            We aim to collect only the information reasonably necessary for the
            purposes described in this policy or otherwise communicated to you
            at the time of collection.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            How We Use Your Information
        </h2>
        <p>
            OnnaSoft may use personal information to respond to inquiries,
            provide requested services, prepare proposals, manage business
            relationships, deliver technical support, and communicate relevant
            updates about our services.
        </p>
        <p>
            We may also use information to maintain website functionality,
            improve our products and services, protect our systems, prevent
            misuse, and comply with applicable legal obligations. Where consent
            is required, we will request it before using information for the
            relevant purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
            We do not intend to use your personal information for purposes
            incompatible with those described in this policy without providing
            appropriate notice or obtaining consent where required by law.
        </p>
    </section>

    <figure class="space-y-3">
        <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1563013544-824ae1b704d3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80"
            alt="Digital security and protection of personal information"
            class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500">
            Responsible data management and security are essential to building
            lasting digital trust.
        </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Data Protection and Security
        </h2>
        <p>
            Protecting information is an important part of our approach to
            technology. OnnaSoft uses appropriate safeguards designed to reduce
            the risk of unauthorized access, accidental disclosure, loss, or
            improper use of personal information.
        </p>
        <p>
            These safeguards may include access controls, secure data handling
            procedures, system monitoring, and other technical or organizational
            measures suited to the nature of the information and the services
            provided. However, no method of data transmission or electronic
            storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
        </p>
        <p>
            We encourage clients and website visitors to use secure
            communication channels and avoid sending sensitive information
            through public or unsecured channels unless specifically necessary
            and appropriate.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Sharing Information with Third Parties
        </h2>
        <p>
            OnnaSoft does not sell personal information as a business practice.
            We may share information with trusted service providers who help us
            operate our website, manage communications, provide technical
            infrastructure, or deliver contracted services.
        </p>
        <p>
            When third parties process information on our behalf, we seek to
            ensure that appropriate safeguards and contractual obligations are
            in place, consistent with applicable law. Information may also be
            disclosed when required by law, necessary to protect rights or
            security, or otherwise permitted under applicable regulations.
        </p>
        <p>
            If information must be transferred internationally, we will take the
            steps required by applicable data protection laws to ensure that the
            transfer is handled appropriately.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Cookies and Website Technologies
        </h2>
        <p>
            Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to support
            essential functionality, remember preferences, analyze traffic, and
            improve performance. The specific technologies used may vary
            depending on the website features and services available.
        </p>
        <p>
            Where required, we will request your consent before using
            non-essential cookies or similar technologies. You can also manage
            cookie preferences through available website controls or your
            browser settings. Disabling certain cookies may affect the
            functionality of some website features.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
            We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably
            necessary to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected,
            maintain our business relationships, meet contractual requirements,
            resolve disputes, and comply with applicable legal obligations.
        </p>
        <p>
            When information is no longer required, we will take reasonable
            steps to delete it, securely dispose of it, or anonymize it, subject
            to any legal or operational requirements that require continued
            retention.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">Your Privacy Rights</h2>
        <p>
            Depending on your location and the laws that apply, you may have the
            right to request access to your personal information, correct
            inaccurate data, request deletion, ask about how your information is
            being processed, withdraw consent where processing relies on
            consent, or exercise other applicable data protection rights.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you are located in Colombia, applicable personal data protection
            rules, including Law 1581 of 2012 and its regulations, may provide
            rights to know, update, and rectify your personal data, request
            evidence of authorization where applicable, obtain information about
            its use, and submit complaints to the competent authority when
            appropriate.
        </p>
        <p>
            Requests can be submitted using the contact details provided below.
            We may need to verify your identity before processing a request and
            will respond within the time limits established by applicable law.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Third-Party Websites and Services
        </h2>
        <p>
            Our website may contain links to third-party websites, platforms, or
            services. These external services operate under their own privacy
            policies and practices, which may differ from ours.
        </p>
        <p>
            We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any external
            website or service you visit. This policy applies to information
            handled by OnnaSoft and does not automatically govern the practices
            of independent third parties.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Updates to This Privacy Policy
        </h2>
        <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in our
            services, data practices, technology, or legal requirements. When
            updates are made, we will publish the revised version on this page
            and update the effective date where appropriate.
        </p>
        <p>
            We encourage you to review this page periodically to stay informed
            about how OnnaSoft handles personal information.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Contact Us About Privacy
        </h2>
        <p>
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, wish to exercise
            your data protection rights, or need more information about how your
            personal information is handled, please contact the OnnaSoft team
            through the contact channels published on our website.
        </p>
        <p>
            We are committed to addressing privacy inquiries responsibly and
            helping you understand how your information is collected, used, and
            protected.
        </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="space-y-3 border-t border-gray-200 pt-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
            Transparency, responsibility, and security guide our approach to
            data privacy.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Effective date: October 29, 2026.</p>
    </footer>
</article>
